# Elusive Otter's block restriction reads its power as it is (CR 509.1b, 613). Casting Mishra's Bauble, a noncreature spell,
# triggers prowess and makes it a 2/2 until end of turn (CR 702.108a), so Bot2's Llanowar Elves (power 1) can no longer block
# it, as well as the Ornithopter (power 0); Cathar Commando (power 3, not less than 2) still can, and the two trade.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Elusive Otter
Mishra's Bauble
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Llanowar Elves
Cathar Commando
Ornithopter
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Elusive Otter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Cathar Commando.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mishra's Bauble.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter.Power = 2
Bot1.Attack(Elusive Otter > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter > Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter)
! Bot2.Block(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves > Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter)
Bot2.Block(Bot2.Battlefield.Cathar Commando > Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Cathar Commando
Bot1.Graveyard = Elusive Otter
